    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141-a1">

                <pb facs="0209" n="141" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg141"/>

                <head>American government vs. Hoffman.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>18 <hi rendition="#small-caps">Trinity House Lane,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Hull,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1887-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 12,1887</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> Our inquiries in Bremen tend so
                    strongly to the conclusion that the prisoner Hoffman was an innocent utterer of
                    the counterfeit notes, that we have thought it our duty to assent to his
                    discharge. The charge against Meana Jackson was also withdrawn. I enclose <pb
                        facs="0210" n="142" xml:id="pg142"/> you copies of the information on which
                    we have acted, which was corroborated by inquiries made through another source.
                    The guilty party is most probably a sailor on board the Atlantic steamship
                    trading to Bremen, and it will be for your government to consider the expediency
                    of prosecuting further inquiries there with a view to the apprehension of the
                    sailor who gave the notes to Hoffman.</p>
                <p>The inquiry here will in all probability be the means of stopping the further
                    circulation of the counterfeit paper in this country. Yours, truly,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ROLLIT &amp; SON.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>H. J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atkinson,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">United States Consul, Hull.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
